---
import '../posters.css';
import AdFooter from '../AdFooter.astro';

export const ad = {
  slug: "sixty-miles",
  title: "“At sixty miles an hour the loudest noise in this picture comes from the concrete.”",
  description: "Ferrari at El Segundo Auto Repair. El Segundo, California.",
  art: "/ad-department/art/el-segundo-ferrari.png",
};
---

<article class="campaign-ad" aria-labelledby="ad-sixty">
  <div class="ad-folio">Advertisement</div>
  <div class="ad-inner">
    <div class="ad-visual">
      <img
        src="/ad-department/art/el-segundo-ferrari.png"
        alt="Gold Ferrari at El Segundo Auto Repair"
        style="width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 50% 78%"
      />
      <img
        src="/ad-department/art/taxi.svg"
        alt="A Noun with a yellow taxi for a head"
        class="noun"
        style="position: absolute; bottom: 0; right: 4%; height: 34%"
      />
    </div>
    <p class="ad-caption">Ferrari at El Segundo Auto Repair. El Segundo, California.</p>
    <h2 id="ad-sixty" class="ad-headline is-long">
      &ldquo;At sixty miles an hour the loudest noise in this picture comes from the
      concrete.&rdquo;
    </h2>
    <div class="ad-copy cols-2">
      <p>
        The car is not moving. It has no need to. A gold Ferrari parked in front of a blue repair
        shop has already arrived wherever it was going.
      </p>
      <p>
        What you hear is the building. Tile, steel sash, four posters pasted flat, a sign
        lettered by somebody who owned a ruler and trusted it.
      </p>
      <p>
        We could describe the engine. Every advertisement does. We would rather you looked at the
        lintel. It has been holding that corner up, without complaint, for longer than the car
        has been out of the shop.
      </p>
    </div>
    <AdFooter>The car is the quiet part.</AdFooter>
  </div>
</article>
